From 1c293e6d3aa6be463703330f832aa49be74b4b82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LNPANDY <lnp-andy@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:46:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gfx: GPU BC1-3 to ASTC 4x4 transcode and BC4-5 compute decode

Transcode BC1-3 textures to ASTC 4x4 (1 B/px) and decode BC4-5 on GPU compute for Metal GPUs without native BC support (A15/A16 and older) across both NVN and Vulkan backends.

- Share one BC1-3 -> ASTC 4x4 encoder body between C and MSL (dm/gfx/tex/bc2astc_body.inc) and encode GPU deswizzle -> barrier -> bca/bcd compute -> barrier -> content blit in up_flush().
- Initialize new ASTC textures with a valid ASTC void-extent zero block (nvn_astc_zero_block), guard compressed textures against render-target attachment, and default BC6H to RGB9E5 (4 B/px) on non-BC GPUs.
- Allow all non-BC iOS devices in front_ios_device_check(), support DM_NO_BC_ASTC=all|bc1|0, per-texture bc3_keep_rgba8.tsv overrides, and DM_TEST_NO_BC=1 testing on Apple Silicon Macs.
- Release all newly allocated compute pipelines, buffers, and caches in dm_gfx_teardown().

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: GPU BC1-3 to ASTC 4x4 transcoding and BC4-5 compute decode for non-BC Apple GPUs (A15/A16 and older), extending the fork-only non-BC fallback
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#180
